Sculpt the **Skyshard Interceptor**, a symmetric forward-swept fighter jet, as a
50x20x76 opaque-voxel model using only the voxel tool.

## How sculpting works

The only way to place a voxel is the `voxel` binary already on your `PATH`. You
build the model by calling it **one operation at a time**, and the ordered list of
operations you issue — recorded to `actions.json` — is your submission.

The volume starts **empty**. Voxels are **opaque** `#rrggbb` colors — there is no
transparency. Each call only appends the operation to `actions.json` and renders
nothing; run `voxel render` when you want to see the model — it meshes the model to
`mesh.glb` and draws the preview PNG `model.png`. An empty log is already in place at
`{{workspace}}`; you produce the preview and mesh yourself by running `voxel render`.

Each operation is an ordinary subcommand with flags, for example:

```
voxel fill-box --x0 26 --y0 6 --z0 10 --x1 33 --y1 13 --z1 70 --color "#8a94a6"
```

Run `voxel --help` to list every operation and `voxel <operation> --help` for one
operation's exact flags — that help text is the authoritative contract. **Run
`voxel render` to (re)draw `model.png`, then read it** to see your progress and
decide what to do next.

